# Coverage (vitest/istanbul report dirs).
#
# ANCHORED, NOT BARE. This was `coverage`, which matches a directory of that name at ANY depth — so it
# swallowed every SOURCE directory that legitimately carries the word, and the repository grew a negation
# per casualty: the `mailwoman coverage` command, cartographer's fog-of-war module, two docs trees. Each
# was found the same way, by `git add` refusing a path whose siblings were already tracked, and the list
# was always one rename behind — the prefix fold added two more (`mailwoman/lib/coverage/`,
# `mailwoman/test/unit/coverage/`) and would have wanted a fifth and sixth negation.
#
# Vitest writes its report to `<root>/coverage` (the default `reportsDirectory`), and nothing writes a
# per-package one, so anchoring the rule to the root covers the real output and stops claiming source.
/coverage/
playwright-report
playwright-traces
test-results
*.lcov
.vitest-attachments
__screenshots__

