## Conventions

### Never commit shell scripts. Use a `.ts` or `.tsx` file instead.
.sh

# tsc -b incremental state (per-workspace tsconfig.tsbuildinfo) — build junk, never committed.
*.tsbuildinfo

# md5 sidecars written by the weights link scripts' freshness guards (`md5FileWithSidecar`) beside
# whatever they hash. A derived cache keyed on mtime — committing one means a fresh checkout can
# carry a hash that disagrees with the file next to it, which is precisely the staleness the guard
# exists to catch.
*.jsonl.md5

# Throwaway benchmark/verification scripts an agent or operator drops beside the code it is
# measuring. Named so they cannot be mistaken for a keeper, and ignored so a wide `git add` cannot
# sweep one into a commit.
*-tmp.ts
*-tmp.tsx

## Subagent-driven-development scratch (ledgers, briefs, review packages) — per-plan, never committed
.superpowers/


# dev-mcp writes its worktree-arm runner here for the life of one mwdev_compare; never commit it
.mwdev-arm-runner.ts

# Wrangler's local secrets for `wrangler dev`; the committed shape is .dev.vars.example
.dev.vars
